# THRONG Agent Standing Rules — Read before any action

## MANDATORY SESSION START
Before writing any code or making any architectural decision:
1. Read THRONG.md §0 (Standing Directives), §3 (Phase History), §4 (Current Experiment)
2. Read docs/THRONG_ARCHIVE.md §Known Failure Modes
3. Do NOT proceed from Antigravity summary alone — it loses scientific context

## HARD PROHIBITIONS
- Never remove the VQ bottleneck from the primary signal channel
- Never wipe checkpoints without explicit Cam approval in the current session
- Never replace GloVe with hand-crafted primitives in the Rosetta Stone
- Never commit architectural changes to THRONG.md as COMPLETE before Cam review
- Never pkill + relaunch without verifying process count afterward with pgrep
- Never interpret ATE = 0 as anything other than: receivers ignore the signal

## WORKFLOW
- Cam sets architecture and science. Will implements and verifies.
- Implementation prompts come AFTER all diagnostic data is gathered.
- Smoke test must explicitly pass before Modal compute is spent.
- All architectural decisions are relayed through the User to Cam first.
